# No check-disable comments

Coding agents MUST NOT disable ESLint, Fallow, TypeScript, or any other check with comments or config suppressions.

## Forbidden (agents)

- `eslint-disable`, `eslint-disable-next-line`, `eslint-disable-line`
- `@ts-ignore`, `@ts-expect-error`, `@ts-nocheck`
- Fallow / knip / biome / oxlint / prettier ignore comments used to silence findings
- File-level or inline suppressions added only to pass pre-commit or CI

## Required instead

1. Fix the underlying error or warning.
2. If a finding seems like a false positive or truly needs a disable, **stop and ask the human user**. Do not add the suppression yourself.
3. Only human developers may approve and add check disables.

Pre-commit hook failures are signals to fix code, not to silence the checker.
